      "body": "Well, I hope the code can be useful. A few pointers though:\r\n- When I was working on that, I was (and still am, but less so) a pretty inexperienced Android programmer\r\n- The code didn't always work on certain file formats and in certain environments (worked particularily well on JPEG files, but not JPG, which, if I understand correctly, are the same thing (see lines [83](https://github.com/openssf/exif-remover-android/blob/master/app/src/main/java/org/openssf/exifremover/MainActivity.java#L83)-[105](https://github.com/openssf/exif-remover-android/blob/master/app/src/main/java/org/openssf/exifremover/MainActivity.java#L105)\r\n- The code is not particularly well done (see point 1), so if you have any issues/don't understand what I was trying to do please let me know\r\n- If you review [the commit history](https://github.com/openssf/exif-remover-android/commits/master/app/src/main/java/org/openssf/exifremover/MainActivity.java) on that file, I tried it with multiple different libraries, such as [Sephiroth74](https://github.com/sephiroth74)'s [ExifInterface](https://github.com/sephiroth74/Android-Exif-Extended) and now, the default Android ExifInterface\r\n\r\nAlso, at some point I plan on turning that (bad) app into a library for simple Exif data removal. I could try and work on that soon if wanted in Signal.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
